._*

# The Discord bot's link store - live data, one per server, never committed (src/discord)
data/discord/

# The trading post's database - live data, created on first boot, never committed (src/server)
data/tradingpost/

# Clan chat channels (ClanChat), written at runtime like the saves and the trading post above.
data/clans/

# the vote ledger (its own sqlite, one per profile) and the live site list, which carries nothing
# secret itself but names which sites this server is listed on. data/vote/sites.example.json IS
# tracked - it is the documentation for the shape.
data/vote/*.sqlite*
data/vote/sites.json

# The web client files, which are put on the server rather than committed: public/client.jar is
# the release jar the browser runs through CheerpJ (src/web.ts), and whatever bundle came with the
# server lives here too. None of it is built from this repository.
public/

# custom (2026-11-02) - what a fuzz run leaves behind: the watchers' findings
# (NODE_BOTS_FUZZ_FILE) and the options that answered with nothing (NODE_DEAD_OPS_FILE). Both are
# per-run output, and both are regenerated by rerunning. The committed artefact of the same work is
# tools/sim/opsweep-baseline.txt, which is a ratchet and IS tracked.
data/fuzz-findings.jsonl
data/dead-ops.jsonl
